1
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,700
This is really neat!

2
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,400
When do we eat?

3
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,819
First, we have to catch some fish.

4
00:00:21,819 --> 00:00:28,900
In order to catch fish, you have to do this.

5
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,400
Here we go.

6
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:35,119
That's it.

7
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:37,600
Then drop it into the water.

8
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,512
All of this comes before eating. OK?

9
00:00:41,512 --> 00:00:44,300
How do you know so much about fishing?

10
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,100
Grandpa taught me.

11
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,000
We spent a lot of time fishing together.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:58,100
Now, the important thing is to get the hook close to the fish.

13
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,300
All right?

14
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:07,900
Like this.

15
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,000
I think I see some fish right under us, Dad.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,900
Oh, not a chance!

17
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,230
I just saw a big one!

18
00:01:14,230 --> 00:01:15,300
Hi, there!

19
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,300
Hi.

20
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:16,500
What's your name?

21
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,059
Albert.

22
00:01:18,059 --> 00:01:18,971
Are you all alone?

23
00:01:18,971 --> 00:01:20,718
Yes, sir.

24
00:01:20,718 --> 00:01:22,000
How old are you, Albert?

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,800
I'm ten.

26
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,017
Where's your father?

27
00:01:27,017 --> 00:01:31,600
He's up there at the lodge.

28
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,500
Does he know you're here?

29
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,300
Yes, sir.

30
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:37,562
OK, Robbie, maybe you should watch him.

31
00:01:37,562 --> 00:01:39,400
The water's pretty deep here.

32
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:47,400
I'll watch him, Dad.

33
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,100
What time is it?

34
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:52,300
It's almost lunchtime, and no fish yet.

35
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:55,300
I can go up to the lodge for some hot dogs and drinks.

36
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,600
No way!

37
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:59,200
We're here to catch our lunch.

38
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:02,700
To catch fish, you need the right magic.

39
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,700
That's right.

40
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:03,900
I forgot!

41
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,700
The right magic.

42
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,400
Do it for Robbie, Dad.

43
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,300
You remember?

44
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,300
Sure. Come on.

45
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:13,700
Well, first, you have to turn your hat around like this.

46
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:18,700
Then you close your eyes and say the magic words.

47
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:27,095
Fish, fish, send me a fish.

48
00:02:27,095 --> 00:02:33,500
Fish, fish, send me a fish.... I got one!

49
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:35,700
See, it works!

50
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,690
It's a big one!

51
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:39,312
Well, it always worked for me, too.

52
00:02:39,312 --> 00:02:49,200
Grandpa, get the net, please!

53
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:50,600
Dad, you got one, too!

54
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,600
You bet I have!

55
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:57,695
Easy, Philip, easy.

56
00:02:57,695 --> 00:03:00,573
Sorry, Dad.

57
00:03:00,573 --> 00:03:05,800
Well, one more and I've got a pair of boots.

58
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,400
You didn't say the magic words.

59
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,100
Robbie's right.

60
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:12,000
Yes, but you did, and we've got our lunch.

61
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Let's build a fire and cook it!

62
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,500
Come on, Albert, you can help us!

63
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,400
I want to stay here and fish.

64
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:29,453
All right, but be careful.

65
00:03:29,453 --> 00:03:30,500
Is it finished yet?

66
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:31,400
I think so.

67
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:35,100
I hope you like your fish well done.

68
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,100
Burned, you mean.

69
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:49,400
Hey, I'm a doctor, not a chef.

70
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:52,300
Help! Help! I can't swim!

71
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,000
Dad! Grandpa! He fell in!

72
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,500
Easy does it, Robbie.

73
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:11,737
That a boy.

74
00:04:11,737 --> 00:04:15,053
That's it.

75
00:04:15,053 --> 00:04:16,300
He's not breathing, Philip!

76
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,226
Robbie, run to the car!

77
00:04:18,226 --> 00:04:19,500
Bring a blanket and my medical bag.

78
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,500
Yes, Dad.

79
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:31,849
Now, come on, son. Come on, son.

80
00:04:31,849 --> 00:04:34,849
Breathe, Albert!
